  "tagline": "Low-latency graph database using sparse matrices, the maintained successor to RedisGraph.",
  "description": "FalkorDB is a property-graph database that represents adjacency as sparse matrices and evaluates Cypher queries with linear algebra (GraphBLAS). It started in 2023 as a fork of RedisGraph after Redis announced that product's end of life, runs as a Redis-compatible server and speaks openCypher, and its core has since been rewritten in Rust for the 5.x/6.x line. It targets GraphRAG and agent memory, with vector and full-text indexes, multi-tenant graphs and a managed cloud. Licensing is SSPL, so it is source-available rather than open source.",
